WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.565
Aunt Judy carried a tote bag.

2
00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:10.737
"Where are you going?" asked Emmy.

3
00:00:10.738 --> 00:00:15.356
"I'm going on an adventure," said Aunt Judy.

4
00:00:15.357 --> 00:00:17.990
She winked at the kids.

5
00:00:17.991 --> 00:00:28.350
"It's a mystery adventure."

6
00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:33.680
The kids followed Aunt Judy to the kitchen.

7
00:00:33.681 --> 00:00:38.590
She got two apples.

8
00:00:38.591 --> 00:00:43.760
"Adventures make me hungry," said Aunt Judy.

9
00:00:43.761 --> 00:00:47.898
"Are you going far?" asked Harry.

10
00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:51.892
Aunt Judy looked out the window.

11
00:00:51.893 --> 00:00:58.548
"As far as you can imagine," she said.

12
00:00:58.549 --> 00:01:06.749
The kids followed Aunt Judy to her closet.

13
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.410
She got her shoes.

14
00:01:10.411 --> 00:01:15.735
"But it's not too far to walk," she said.

15
00:01:15.736 --> 00:01:19.985
Aunt Judy put on a sweater.

16
00:01:19.986 --> 00:01:25.360
"It's an outside adventure."

17
00:01:25.361 --> 00:01:30.413
"Will you meet wild animals?" asked Oliver.

18
00:01:30.414 --> 00:01:34.260
"Hmm," said Aunt Judy.

19
00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:38.381
"It's possible."

20
00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:41.471
Emmy looked worried.

21
00:01:41.472 --> 00:01:45.086
"Will there be danger?" she asked.

22
00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:51.033
"Oh yes," said Aunt Judy.

23
00:01:51.034 --> 00:01:57.711
"Mystery adventures are always dangerous."

24
00:01:57.712 --> 00:02:03.603
Aunt Judy put on her hat.

25
00:02:03.604 --> 00:02:06.885
"But don't worry," she said.

26
00:02:06.886 --> 00:02:15.688
"I'll meet new friends."

27
00:02:15.689 --> 00:02:18.881
Oliver hugged Aunt Judy.

28
00:02:18.882 --> 00:02:22.254
"We'll miss you," he said.

29
00:02:22.255 --> 00:02:28.352
"You can all come with me," said Aunt Judy.

30
00:02:28.353 --> 00:02:33.229
She pulled something from her bag.

31
00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.458
It was a book.

32
00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:44.135
"I'm going outside to read."

33
00:02:44.136 --> 00:02:48.251
"I want to come!" said Oliver.

34
00:02:48.252 --> 00:02:52.876
"Me too!" said Emmy and Harry.

35
00:02:52.877 --> 00:03:01.146
They all ran to get their books.

